msgid "A concerned citizen wants to scrape together some semblance of a fighting force for Azamire's defense against any would-be bandits or those black-robed figures looking to finish the job, but she's barely in fighting shape herself."
msgstr "一位憂心的市民想湊出一支像樣的戰鬥隊伍，保衛 Azamire 免受強盜或那些想斬草除根的黑袍人侵擾，但她自己的身體狀況也幾乎無法作戰。"

msgid "Just putting some pointy rocks on some wood, nothing too tough."
msgstr "只是把尖石頭綁在木頭上而已，沒什麼難的。"

msgid "I think they've gotten the idea."
msgstr "我想他們已經懂了。"

msgid "The cinders from the assault on Azamire have only just fizzled out, much like many of the survivors' will to go on. Everyone that remained had lost something. Their homes. Family members. Friends. You and [Companion Name] sit on the soot covered cobbles that once made up the town's main thoroughfare, watching another family carry what little they have left and shuffle out of town, hoping that some nearby village may have been spared. Neither of you blame them.\n\nA woman with a bloodied stump where her hand should have been approaches the two of you and falls to the ground beside you with a sigh."
msgstr "Azamire 遭襲後的餘燼才剛熄滅，許多倖存者活下去的意志也一樣。留下來的每個人都失去了些什麼。家園、家人、朋友。你和 [Companion Name] 坐在曾是鎮上主要大道、如今滿是煤灰的鵝卵石上，看著又一戶人家帶著僅剩的家當，拖著腳步離開小鎮，盼望附近某個村莊能倖免於難。你們都不怪他們。\n\n一名女子走向你們，她的手本該在的地方只剩下血淋淋的斷肢。她嘆了口氣，在你們身旁坐倒在地。"

msgid "Well. You two headed out as well?"
msgstr "唉。你們兩個也要走了？"

msgid "I can't turn my back on Azamire. Too many folks have done too much for me, growing up."
msgstr "我不能背棄 Azamire。我從小到大，太多人為我付出太多了。"

msgid "Doubt many of 'em are left."
msgstr "我懷疑他們還剩下多少人。"

msgid "The town still is, though."
msgstr "但小鎮還在。"

msgid "Not much of it."
msgstr "也剩沒多少了。"

msgid "I take it you're leaving, then? Can't blame you, but this is home for the both of us. Even if... Home's looking a little worse for wear."
msgstr "看來妳要離開了？我不怪妳，但這裡是我們倆的家。即使……家看起來有點殘破了。"

msgid "Gods no! No shame to those who are, but those rotters took more than just my hand. Teri... didn't make it."
msgstr "老天，當然不是！要走的人沒什麼好丟臉的，但那些混蛋奪走的不只是我的手。Teri……他沒能撐過來。"

msgid "Oh Jass... I'm so sorry."
msgstr "噢，Jass……我很遺憾。"

msgid "Fool of a man got between me and one of those wretches' beasts. Seemed like he was going to pull through... but then he didn't."
msgstr "那個傻男人擋在我和那些惡徒的野獸之間。原本看起來他撐得過去……但最後還是沒有。"

msgid "...We'll make them pay, Jass. [Companion Name] and I won't let this go unanswered."
msgstr "……我們會讓他們付出代價的，Jass。我和 [Companion Name] 不會就這樣算了。"

msgid "You're not alone in your sentiment. I came by to see if you two might be interested in a little project."
msgstr "有這種想法的不只你們。我來是想看看你們兩個會不會對一個小計畫有興趣。"

msgid "A couple of people who aren't running for the hills want to fight back. But they're farmers. Builders."
msgstr "有幾個沒逃走的人想要反擊。但他們是農夫、工匠。"

msgid "I used to be pretty good with a bow, but it'd be a bit tough with this hand... or lack thereof."
msgstr "我以前弓箭用得還不錯，但這隻手……或者說沒有這隻手，會有點困難。"

msgid "Want us to show them the ropes? Been a little while since I shot a bow, but I can show a couple of farmers where to point it and how not to shoot their friends."
msgstr "要我們教他們入門嗎？我有一陣子沒射箭了，但我可以教幾個農夫該往哪瞄，還有怎麼不射到自己的朋友。"

msgid "...Are you forgetting what happened a couple of years ago? I still feel the need to duck every time you-"
msgstr "……你忘了幾年前發生的事了嗎？每次你一拉弓我還是會想趴下——"

msgid "Okay, fine, [Player Name] can do the teaching, maybe I'll learn something too. Is there anything else that I could help with?"
msgstr "好啦好啦，讓 [Player Name] 來教，說不定我也能學到點東西。還有什麼我能幫忙的嗎？"

msgid "Actually, yes. Like I said, most of these folks hardly know anything outside of their trade. Showing them how to put together a couple of arrows could go a long way towards making them self-sufficient."
msgstr "其實有。就像我說的，這些人大多除了自己的本行之外幾乎什麼都不懂。教他們怎麼做幾支箭，對讓他們自給自足會很有幫助。"

msgid "The three of you chat back and forth for a while, putting together the idea of a lesson plan, putting up some ramshackle targets meant to resemble a humanoid figure, and some scavenged gear. Jass brings back a dozen or so dusty villagers from town who seem to carry a wide range of emotions. Some, determined to fight back against the cloaked figures who destroyed the town, some who looked lost and aimless, and some somewhere in between.\n\n[Companion Name] takes half of them and gets to work showing them how to make bows, something they were always better at than actually firing them, while you take the other half and get to work showing them how to make arrows."
msgstr "你們三個來回討論了一陣子，擬出了一份教學計畫，架起幾個勉強像人形的簡陋靶子，還湊了些撿來的裝備。Jass 從鎮上帶回十幾個灰頭土臉的村民，他們的情緒各不相同。有些人決心向摧毀小鎮的斗篷人反擊，有些人看起來茫然無措，還有些介於兩者之間。\n\n[Companion Name] 帶走一半的人，開始教他們製作弓——這向來是他們比實際射箭更擅長的事——而你則帶著另一半，開始教他們製作箭矢。"

msgid "If I didn't know better, I'd say they were aiming at me."
msgstr "要不是我比較清楚，我會說他們在瞄準我。"

msgid "I knew they'd be bad, but wow."
msgstr "我知道他們會很爛，但哇。"

msgid "Many of the folks picked up your teaching pretty quickly. Even Jass, just managing with a single hand, did a fine job putting together some flight-worthy arrows. [Companion Name]'s lesson seemed to go about as smoothly, and they produced a few bows to share amongst themselves for the next bout of training. The villagers quietly, but excitedly, show off what they managed to make, or laugh about how poorly their creations turned out, depending on their results."
msgstr "許多人很快就學會了你教的東西。就連只用一隻手的 Jass，也做出了幾支能飛的箭。[Companion Name] 的課似乎也進行得差不多順利，他們做出了幾把弓，供下一輪訓練時大家輪流使用。村民們安靜卻興奮地展示自己的成果，或是依結果而定，笑著自己的作品做得有多糟。"

msgid "Thank you two for all of this, by the way."
msgstr "順帶一提，謝謝你們兩個做的這一切。"

msgid "Of course. It'll be important for us to not get caught out like this again."
msgstr "當然。我們不能再像這樣措手不及了。"

msgid "This group has a long way to go, still. We had guards, but they lasted all of a few minutes before those things started cutting through the town."
msgstr "這群人還有很長的路要走。我們之前有守衛，但那些東西開始在鎮上大開殺戒後，他們沒撐幾分鐘就倒下了。"

msgid "It's a start, though. And besides, keeping these people busy is just as important as making sure they're trained."
msgstr "不過這是個開始。再說，讓這些人有事可忙，跟確保他們受過訓練一樣重要。"

msgid "Dwelling on everything that happened... Well, that's no good for anyone."
msgstr "一直沉湎於發生過的事……那對誰都沒好處。"

msgid "Anyway. Shall we get to shooting?"
msgstr "總之，我們開始射箭吧？"

msgid "As long as [Companion Name] doesn't stick me with an arrow, sure."
msgstr "只要 [Companion Name] 不拿箭射我就好。"

msgid "[Companion Name] glares at you, but you've known them long enough to know there's no real anger there, just like they know you have no malice in your light banter.\n\nThough, you start to think otherwise when the villagers pick up their bows and start trying to hit the targets. You feel as though their arrows pass by you more often than the targets. You get to work quickly, trying to show them how to draw, aim, and fire, before they really hurt someone."
msgstr "[Companion Name] 瞪了你一眼，但你們相識夠久，你知道那眼神裡沒有真正的怒意，就像對方也知道你輕鬆的玩笑話不帶惡意。\n\n不過，當村民們拿起弓開始試著射靶時，你開始改變想法了。你覺得他們的箭從你身邊飛過的次數比射向靶子還多。你趕緊動手，在他們真的傷到人之前，教他們如何拉弓、瞄準和放箭。"

msgid "You certainly lost a bit of skin from arrows that passed by a bit too close for comfort, but after a while, the villagers' shots start to resemble straight flight paths. A couple folks pick it up faster than the others, among them, [Companion Name], though you still could hardly say you felt safe just yet.\n\nInitially, Jass seemed to be a bit frustrated at not being able to join in the demonstration, but fell into her own role guiding people and repeating your instructions to those that seemed to struggle the first few times around, or giving pointers that even you started to incorporate into your own shots.\n\nBy the end of the day, the villagers didn't seem to actively be putting one another in danger, and looked far more determined than they did at the start of the drill, and you entrust them into Jass's tutelage, for better or worse."
msgstr "有些箭擦身而過，近得讓人不太舒服，你確實因此掉了點皮，但過了一陣子，村民們射出的箭開始有了筆直的軌跡。有幾個人學得比別人快，[Companion Name] 也是其中之一，不過你還是很難說自己已經覺得安全了。\n\n一開始，Jass 似乎因為無法參與示範而有些沮喪，但她很快找到了自己的角色：引導大家，向前幾輪似乎有困難的人重複你的指示，甚至給出連你都開始在自己射擊時採用的建議。\n\n到了傍晚，村民們看起來已經不會主動讓彼此陷入危險，而且比訓練開始時堅定得多。無論好壞，你把他們託付給 Jass 指導。"

msgid "Fishin' for Trouble"
msgstr "釣出麻煩"

msgid "While out on a fishing trip, a little girl has gone missing with only her fishing pole and a single tooth left behind. Not much to go on, except one small detail. It isn't a human tooth."
msgstr "一個小女孩外出釣魚時失蹤了，只留下她的釣竿和一顆牙齒。線索不多，只有一個小細節：那不是人類的牙齒。"

msgid "Swords are plenty sharp, that'll do."
msgstr "劍夠鋒利了，這樣就行。"

msgid "Let's hope they can figure out how to swing 'em."
msgstr "希望他們搞得懂怎麼揮劍。"

msgid "You just start to drift off to sleep before a frantic pounding at your door makes you jump up and start grabbing for something nearby to protect yourself. Your door opens a bit more gently than you'd expect considering the knocking, and you find [Companion Name] looking worried with a young woman behind her. She holds up something about as thick as your finger with a sickly pale yellow hue."
msgstr "你才剛要入睡，一陣急促的敲門聲就讓你跳了起來，伸手去抓身邊能防身的東西。考慮到那陣敲門聲，門被打開的力道比你預期的溫和許多，你看到 [Companion Name] 一臉憂心，身後站著一名年輕女子。她舉起一個約有你手指粗、泛著病態淡黃色的東西。"

msgid "Her daughter was out fishing near the river and didn't come home for dinner. Sorry to interrupt your sleep, but I figured you'd want to help."
msgstr "她女兒在河邊釣魚，晚餐時間都沒回家。抱歉打擾你睡覺，但我想你會想幫忙。"

msgid "You're not wrong. And the thing you're holding?"
msgstr "你說得沒錯。那你手上拿的是？"

msgid "Golbin tooth. The only... blood, that was there was blue, so..."
msgstr "哥布林的牙齒。那裡唯一的……血跡是藍色的，所以……"

msgid "The girl is okay, at least for now, I'd imagine."
msgstr "我想那女孩沒事，至少目前是。"

msgid "Good, good. Then, just the two of us are headed out?"
msgstr "很好，很好。那就只有我們兩個出發？"

msgid "Thankfully, no. Jass has been making a bit of progress with her 'militia' and they want to join us."
msgstr "還好不是。Jass 的「民兵」有了點進展，他們想跟我們一起去。"

msgid "It's anyone's guess how many Golbins there will be. It'd be smart to let them come to us."
msgstr "沒人知道會有多少哥布林。讓他們主動找上我們會比較聰明。"

msgid "What if we set the same scene as... the incident, have have Jass's people waiting for them?"
msgstr "如果我們重現……事發時的場景，讓 Jass 的人埋伏等著他們呢？"

msgid "Just please... hurry. I'm hopeful my little Ana is safe, but... it's not like they took her for a fun little stroll around the woods. I know she must be so frightened..."
msgstr "拜託……快一點。我希望我的小 Ana 平安無事，但……他們又不是帶她去樹林裡悠閒散步。我知道她一定很害怕……"

msgid "Don't worry, we'll do everything that we can."
msgstr "別擔心，我們會盡一切努力。"

msgid "You gather your things and leave your bed behind, meeting up with Jass and a couple of folks just outside. Some of them hold the bows [Companion Name] helped them make, some holding new ones they must have created themselves. However, any decent force has variety - archers wouldn't fare well if the Golbins got in their ranks - and their inventiveness hasn't improved in the short time since you helped them last. Jass asks for a couple of new toys for the folks that haven't taken well to the bow."
msgstr "你收拾好東西離開床鋪，在門外與 Jass 和幾個人會合。有些人拿著 [Companion Name] 幫他們做的弓，有些人拿著自己新做的。然而，任何像樣的隊伍都需要多樣性——如果哥布林衝進隊伍裡，弓箭手可撐不了多久——而自從你上次幫忙後，他們的創造力在短短時間內並沒有進步。Jass 請你為那些不擅長用弓的人做幾件新玩具。"

msgid "Just catch some fish and don't look suspicious. Easy."
msgstr "釣幾條魚，別看起來可疑就好。簡單。"

msgid "What was that?"
msgstr "那是什麼？"

msgid "The folks take up their new weapons eagerly. Though it has only been a short time since Jass gathered them, the combined militia now totaled a couple dozen. You notice as you hand out swords, though most don't have any conventional fighting experience, these people tend to lean capable. Lumber Workers and farmers who've built functional bodies through years of hard labour. Against a trained fighting force, sure, they'd hardly stand a chance. But against a group of ragtag Golbins? You like their odds."
msgstr "大家熱切地拿起新武器。雖然 Jass 召集他們才沒多久，整支民兵已有二十幾人。你在發放劍時注意到，雖然大多數人沒有正規的戰鬥經驗，但這些人頗有能耐。伐木工和農夫們經過多年粗活，練就了結實的身體。對上訓練有素的軍隊，他們當然毫無勝算。但對上一群烏合之眾的哥布林？你覺得他們勝算不小。"

msgid "Jass, you sure about this?"
msgstr "Jass，妳確定嗎？"

msgid "They might not have much experience, but the folks that couldn't hit the broad side of a barn - or just otherwise hated trying to use the bows - I've had running drills with sticks and leftover tools."
msgstr "他們也許經驗不多，但那些連穀倉大門都射不中的人——或是就是討厭用弓的人——我已經讓他們拿棍子和剩下的工具練習過了。"

msgid "They got a long way to go, but they know enough to hold their own. I'm not sending them in to die, don't worry."
msgstr "他們還有很長的路要走，但已經足以自保。我不會派他們去送死的，別擔心。"

msgid "Good, good. Azamire can't get much smaller if we want to keep calling ourselves a town. "
msgstr "很好，很好。如果我們還想自稱是個小鎮，Azamire 可不能再小下去了。 "

msgid "If this ambush goes well, they won't need to fight much. Just need to look scary and grab one of two of the Golbins to tell us where they brought the girl."
msgstr "如果這次伏擊順利，他們就不需要怎麼戰鬥。只要看起來嚇人，然後抓一兩隻哥布林問出他們把女孩帶去哪裡就好。"

msgid "If everyone's ready, let's head out to the river, then?"
msgstr "如果大家都準備好了，那我們就出發去河邊吧？"

msgid "[Companion Name] leads you to the river where the girl went missing. You fondly recall learning to swim with [Companion Name] here, years ago, and wish you were here under less dire circumstances. The militia disperses through the surrounding forest, headed by Jass who quietly gives orders, trying to get people hidden as best she can.\n\nYou and [Companion Name] settle in by the riverbank, and pull out your rods, hoping to catch a bit more than just a few fish. You're a bit too nervous for idle conversation, so you both quietly fall into a rhythm, just trying to look like two innocuous people fishing late into the night."
msgstr "[Companion Name] 帶你來到女孩失蹤的河邊。你懷念地想起多年前和 [Companion Name] 在這裡學游泳的時光，真希望這次來不是在如此危急的情況下。民兵們在 Jass 的帶領下分散到周圍的森林中，她低聲下達命令，盡可能讓大家藏好。\n\n你和 [Companion Name] 在河岸邊坐下，拿出釣竿，希望釣到的不只是幾條魚。你緊張得無心閒聊，於是你們倆都安靜地進入節奏，只是盡量看起來像兩個深夜釣魚的無害路人。"

msgid "I'm not going to let [Companion Name] beat me!"
msgstr "我可不會讓 [Companion Name] 贏過我！"

msgid "That should be about all of them."
msgstr "應該差不多就這些了。"

msgid "You worry for a moment that one of the militia members is being too loud before you see it. A group of Golbins, sauntering up with hardly a care in the world, barking orders at one another, trying to surround you and [Companion Name]. It's... more than you expected, and as you start to get up to defend yourself, an arrow sinks right between the leading Golbin's shoulder blades. "
msgstr "你一度擔心有民兵發出太大聲響，接著就看到了。一群哥布林大搖大擺地走過來，毫不在意，互相吆喝著命令，試圖包圍你和 [Companion Name]。數量……比你預期的多，就在你起身準備自衛時，一支箭正中帶頭哥布林的兩肩胛骨之間。 "

msgid "Everyone, now!"
msgstr "大家，就是現在！"

msgid "Make sure to leave a couple breathing!"
msgstr "記得留幾個活口！"

msgid "Bet you I'll kill more than you. Try not to die."
msgstr "我打賭我殺得比你多。盡量別死啊。"

msgid "You're on."
msgstr "一言為定。"

msgid "[Companion Name]'s look of anxiety hidden under bravado is quickly replaced with confidence as the woods explode with movement. The militia lets loose a volley of arrows that pepper the unprepared Golbins, scattering them and sending a few more to the ground. What's left of them gather themselves and charge towards you and your friend, or the quickly approaching villagers armed with swords."
msgstr "隨著樹林中爆發出一陣騷動，[Companion Name] 隱藏在逞強之下的焦慮神情，很快就被自信取代。民兵射出一波箭雨，打得毫無防備的哥布林四處逃竄，又有幾隻倒地。剩下的哥布林重整旗鼓，衝向你和你的朋友，或是那些手持長劍、迅速逼近的村民。"

msgid "You look around as the movement begins to settle. The Golbin force was larger than you had anticipated, but your efforts went as well as could be expected. Among the bodies littering the forest floor, from what you could see, only a couple were human, which was better than expected considering their experience.\n\nYou rush over as you hear a shout from Jass, who managed to pin a dark green Golbin to ground. The beast would have hardly came up to your hip had it been on its feet, and you could hear it whimpering and begging not to be hurt. It quickly rattles off fragments of information that it thinks could be useful, detailing how its clan was taken over by a rival group led by someone it called the 'Ringleader', its own name - Gloob - and how it really really wants to live. Jass slaps her hand over its mouth and asks it where the girl they kidnapped was, and why they took her. Gloob goes one step further, and says that it'll lead you all there to its nearby camp, and that they were going to try and paint him and sell him off too, whatever that may mean.\n\nYou discuss it briefly together, and decide to 'trust' it to do as it says. Surely enough, the camp is close, and the leftover defenders quickly scatter as they see they're vastly outnumbered, leaving their camp behind. You and [Companion Name] quickly find Ana in one of their tents and take her home, while Jass and the militia handle a dozen or so other folks who had been captured from elsewhere throughout the countryside. Ana's mother meets you just outside of Azamire with tears in her eyes, thanking you over and over again for saving her daughter."
msgstr "騷動漸漸平息，你環顧四周。哥布林的兵力比你預料的還多，但你們的行動已經順利得超乎預期。就你所見，散落在林地上的屍體中只有幾具是人類，以他們的經驗而言，這比預期好多了。\n\n聽到 Jass 的喊聲，你急忙趕過去，她成功把一隻深綠色的哥布林壓在地上。這傢伙站起來恐怕也不到你的腰，你能聽到牠嗚咽著求饒。牠飛快地吐出一些自認有用的零碎情報，說明牠的部族被一個由牠稱為「首領」的傢伙所帶領的敵對團體吞併，還說了自己的名字——Gloob——以及牠真的真的很想活下去。Jass 一手摀住牠的嘴，問牠被綁走的女孩在哪裡、為什麼要綁走她。Gloob 更進一步，說牠會帶你們去附近的營地，還說他們本來也打算把牠塗上顏色賣掉，不管那是什麼意思。\n\n你們簡短地討論了一下，決定「相信」牠會照說的做。果然，營地就在附近，殘餘的守衛一看到自己寡不敵眾就迅速四散逃跑，丟下了營地。你和 [Companion Name] 很快在其中一頂帳篷裡找到 Ana 並帶她回家，而 Jass 和民兵則負責處理十幾個從鄉間各地被抓來的其他人。Ana 的母親在 Azamire 外迎接你們，眼中含淚，一次又一次地感謝你們救了她的女兒。"

msgid "Boarish Bonfire"
msgstr "野豬篝火"

msgid "Azamire has slowly but surely begun to get back onto its feet, and that's cause for celebration. The town's impromptu mayor, Hapren, has thought of just the thing to get folks together, a bit of warmth and food in the center of town."
msgstr "Azamire 已經緩慢但穩定地開始重新站起來，這值得慶祝。鎮上臨時的鎮長 Hapren 想到了一個能讓大家聚在一起的好點子：在鎮中心來點溫暖和食物。"

msgid "A little cleanup could go a long way to making things feel a bit more put together."
msgstr "稍微清理一下，就能讓這裡看起來整齊許多。"

msgid "Looking a lot nicer."
msgstr "看起來好多了。"

msgid "A handful of people you haven't seen before walk past, likely another group of refugees from one of the nearby villages that fared even worse than Azamire, attacked around the same time. The town's new mayor - the son of the previous mayor that was lost in the attack - welcomes them and directs them towards one of the newly repaired buildings that they were using to shelter people before more buildings could be made to house them. Once he wraps up, he sets his eyes on you and [Companion Name]."
msgstr "幾個你從沒見過的人走過，可能是附近某個村莊的另一批難民，那裡大約在同一時間遭到襲擊，下場比 Azamire 更慘。鎮上的新鎮長——在襲擊中喪生的前任鎮長之子——歡迎他們，並指引他們前往一棟剛修好的建築，在蓋好更多房屋之前，那裡被用來收容人們。他處理完後，便將目光投向你和 [Companion Name]。"

msgid "Hey there, you two. I hope that things have been as good as they can be, considering..."
msgstr "嘿，你們兩個。希望一切都還算好，考慮到……"

msgid "Everything?"
msgstr "所有的事？"

msgid "Exactly... There's no easy way to put such a tragedy, huh?"
msgstr "沒錯……這種悲劇真的很難用三言兩語說清楚，對吧？"

msgid "There really isn't. You inherited quite the mess, didn't you?"
msgstr "確實。你接手了一個大爛攤子，不是嗎？"

msgid "Don't suppose either of you would be willing to take over, would you?"
msgstr "我想你們兩個應該都不願意接手吧？"

msgid "Afraid not. Never had the decorum to fit into a role like that. "
msgstr "恐怕不行。我從來就沒有擔任那種角色的禮數。 "

msgid "Didn't figure. Well, would you two mind helping me out with a little project, then?"
msgstr "我想也是。那麼，你們兩個介意幫我一個小忙嗎？"

msgid "What do you have in mind, exactly?"
msgstr "你具體在想什麼？"

msgid "Hapren brings the two of you over to the center of town, which has been piled with debris from Azamire's cleanup efforts. He talks about how he'd love to throw a little gathering for the town, just so folks can get to know one another and feel a bit of normalcy despite how hard the last while has been. A few people try their best to break down the rubble into movable chunks, but progress is slow, and Hapren asks for help before starting to work on the pile himself."
msgstr "Hapren 帶你們兩個來到鎮中心，那裡堆滿了 Azamire 清理工作留下的瓦礫。他說他很想為鎮上辦個小聚會，好讓大家互相認識，在最近這段艱難的日子裡感受一點日常。有幾個人盡力把瓦礫敲成能搬動的碎塊，但進展緩慢，Hapren 在親自動手處理之前先請你們幫忙。"

msgid "Nothing too flashy, just gotta pull up enough fish to show them how it's done."
msgstr "不用太花俏，只要釣上足夠的魚，示範給他們看就行了。"

msgid "Huh, there really is a lot of junk in the water. Wonder where it's coming from?"
msgstr "咦，水裡真的有好多垃圾。不知道是從哪來的？"

msgid "With you and [Companion Name]'s help, you manage to break up the debris in short order, and Hapren directs much of the salvageable materials to be stored for reconstruction efforts, and the wood that is too mangled to be used to be left in the square to be used for the bonfire.\n\nJust as you set your tools down, a few tired looking folks make their way into the center of town, fishing gear in hand."
msgstr "在你和 [Companion Name] 的幫助下，你們很快就把瓦礫清理完畢。Hapren 指示將大部分可回收的材料存放起來供重建使用，至於損壞得無法使用的木頭，則留在廣場上當作篝火的柴薪。\n\n就在你放下工具時，幾個看起來疲憊不堪的人拿著釣具走進了鎮中心。"

msgid "If I couldn't see them swimming around, I'd swear the stock of fish had run dry."
msgstr "要不是我看得到牠們在游，我會發誓魚都被釣光了。"

msgid "Feels like we're pullin' more junk out of the water than fish."
msgstr "感覺我們從水裡拉上來的垃圾比魚還多。"

msgid "Rough day?"
msgstr "今天不順？"

msgid "You could say that. I see that the town square is just about ready, but I'm sorry... It'll take us a week to have enough fish at this rate."
msgstr "可以這麼說。我看到廣場差不多準備好了，但很抱歉……照這個速度，我們要一個禮拜才能湊到足夠的魚。"

msgid "Wait, you're using Mackerel Bait, right? Only way I've managed to pull anything out of there."
msgstr "等等，你們用的是鯖魚魚餌吧？那是我唯一能從那裡釣到東西的方法。"

msgid "...No. Honestly, don't think I've ever used much more than a worm, really."
msgstr "……沒有。老實說，我好像從來沒用過蚯蚓以外的東西。"

msgid "Well, you don't need it, but it sure doesn't hurt."
msgstr "嗯，不一定需要，但用了絕對沒壞處。"

msgid "Since we're just about done here... While we get things set up, would you mind lending them a hand?"
msgstr "既然我們這邊差不多好了……在我們布置的時候，你們介意幫他們一把嗎？"

msgid "[Companion Name] looks to you and searches your face, trying to gauge your reaction. You shrug, and then offer to help. Getting together a bit of bait to help the fishers out, then showing them how to work with the river shouldn't take too long, and it'd be nice for the town to be able to keep itself fed."
msgstr "[Companion Name] 看著你，打量你的表情，想知道你的反應。你聳聳肩，然後主動表示願意幫忙。準備一些魚餌幫助漁夫，再教他們如何應對這條河，應該花不了多少時間，而且如果鎮上能自給自足會很不錯。"

msgid "There's no helping it, then!"
msgstr "那就沒辦法了！"

msgid "Maybe Hapren would appreciate the meat?"
msgstr "也許 Hapren 會想要這些肉？"

msgid "You all spend awhile on the pebble bank, sitting and waiting for a fish to bite, as one typically does while fishing. You and [Companion Name] talk to the fishermen for a while and learn that they used to be able to pull out enough fish to feed half the town, even without the bait. When you dump bait in the water, and start using some on your hooks, things pick up, but it's still rather slow. You watch even more junk float by. Bits of tree branches, huge clumps of soil, and then, a dead Golbin. The fishers point out that it's been like this for a few days, minus the Golbins at least."
msgstr "你們在卵石河岸上待了好一陣子，坐著等魚上鉤，就像釣魚時常有的那樣。你和 [Companion Name] 跟漁夫們聊了一會兒，得知他們以前就算不用魚餌，也能釣到足夠餵飽半個鎮的魚。當你把魚餌撒進水裡，並開始在魚鉤上使用時，情況有所好轉，但還是相當緩慢。你看著更多垃圾漂過。樹枝碎片、大塊泥土，然後是一隻死掉的哥布林。漁夫們指出，這種情況已經持續好幾天了，至少哥布林是第一次。"

msgid "Something must be going on up river, this is just odd."
msgstr "上游一定發生了什麼事，這太奇怪了。"

msgid "You all can keep fishing. Try not to reel in... anything green."
msgstr "你們繼續釣吧。盡量別釣到……任何綠色的東西。"

msgid "You're going to go check it out, aren't you?"
msgstr "你要去查看一下，對吧？"

msgid "Of course we are. You're coming too, obviously. Unless you want to see me floating by, next?"
msgstr "當然。你也要來，這還用說。除非你想下次看到我漂過去？"

msgid "I haven't shown them how I usually tie my hooks yet, I really-"
msgstr "我還沒示範我平常怎麼綁魚鉤，我真的——"

msgid "They stop their protesting as you grab their shoulder and pull them behind you. You know from all your time together they'd never really let you go by yourself, but as they grumble behind you, it's clear they're not pleased about running off to find... whatever is, up river.\n\nAfter a few minute jaunt upstream, you see it. A massive boar standing over a group of dead Golbins. It pulls against ropes that had been tied to trees along the river, and then thrown over the top of the beast. As you approach it catches sight of you both, assumes and breaks the last of its restrains as it charges towards you!"
msgstr "你抓住對方的肩膀把人拉到身後，對方這才停止抗議。從你們相處的這些時間，你知道對方絕不會真的讓你一個人去，但聽著身後的嘀咕聲，顯然對方對於跑去上游找……不管那是什麼，並不太高興。\n\n往上游走了幾分鐘後，你看到了。一頭巨大的野豬站在一群死掉的哥布林旁。牠拉扯著綁在河邊樹上、再拋過牠身上的繩索。當你們靠近時，牠發現了你們，掙斷最後的束縛，朝你們衝了過來！"

msgid "With the help of some villagers and their carts, you manage to bring back the Golbin's pet taming project. Hapren is shocked, then pleased, as he realizes that this is a far better catch than a few fish from the river.\n\nAs the sun sets, the wooden debris from the square is burnt and thick slabs of boar are grilled and given out to everyone in attendance. More and more curious folks poke their heads into the square and are met with warmth and light conversation.  A few folks even start up with light songs as the night progresses and Azamire's paltry stores of booze are enjoyed by those who indulge.\n\nAzamire's attack is far from forgotten, but this quiet moment amongst the survivors does well to begin healing the towns aching wounds."
msgstr "在一些村民和他們的推車協助下，你們成功把哥布林的寵物馴服計畫帶了回來。Hapren 先是震驚，接著很高興，因為他意識到這比從河裡釣到的幾條魚要好得多。\n\n夕陽西下時，廣場上的木頭瓦礫被點燃，厚厚的野豬肉片被烤好分給每一位到場的人。越來越多好奇的人探頭進廣場，迎接他們的是溫暖與輕鬆的談話。隨著夜色漸深，有些人甚至唱起了輕快的歌，願意小酌的人則享用著 Azamire 少得可憐的酒類存貨。\n\nAzamire 遭受的襲擊遠未被遺忘，但倖存者之間這片刻的寧靜，為小鎮痛楚的傷口開始癒合帶來了很大的幫助。"

msgid "Misty Reconnaissance"
msgstr "迷霧偵察"

msgid "Gloob and Jass have been 'working' together for a while, and now need your help to launch a daring mission... or stupidly walk into a Golbin's trap."
msgstr "Gloob 和 Jass 已經「合作」了一段時間，現在需要你協助展開一項大膽的任務……或是愚蠢地走進哥布林的陷阱。"

msgid "I should be able to follow Gloob's schematics easy enough."
msgstr "我應該能輕鬆照著 Gloob 的設計圖做。"

msgid "These should work!"
msgstr "這些應該行得通！"

msgid "As you walk back into Azamire, you feel a swell of pride at the number of newly constructed buildings. They're small, and you hardly takes you long to count them on two hands, but still, Azamire is rebuilding, bit by bit.\n\nYour delight is interrupted by a shriek as you hear a... Golbin run by, chased by the newly appointed Militia Captain - Jass. The chase doesn't last long, and Gloob is held down while Jass berates it, talking about how she's no fool and knows a trap when she sees one."
msgstr "當你走回 Azamire 時，看著那些新蓋好的建築，你心中湧起一股自豪。它們很小，兩隻手就數得完，但無論如何，Azamire 正一點一點地重建。\n\n你的喜悅被一聲尖叫打斷，你聽見一隻……哥布林跑過，被新任命的民兵隊長——Jass——追著跑。追逐沒持續多久，Gloob 就被壓制在地，Jass 一邊斥責牠，一邊說自己可不是傻瓜，看得出什麼是陷阱。"

msgid "I see that things are going well."
msgstr "看來事情進展得很順利嘛。"

msgid "SHE'S GOING TO EAT ME, PLEASE HELP!"
msgstr "她要吃掉我，救命啊！"

msgid "We're keeping you here because you were meant to help us, beast!"
msgstr "我們把你留在這裡是因為你應該要幫我們，你這畜生！"

msgid "What I said was true! You should be able to sneak into the Ringleader's fortress at night, it'd be fine!"
msgstr "我說的是真的！你們晚上應該能潛入首領的堡壘，不會有事的！"

msgid "The guards have wood for brains! You'll see what I mean!"
msgstr "那些守衛腦袋都是木頭做的！你們看了就知道我的意思！"

msgid "We'll do no such thing! We ought to string you up for what your little pack did to Ana!"
msgstr "我們才不會那麼做！你那一小群同夥對 Ana 做的事，我們應該把你吊起來才對！"

msgid "What's happening, exactly?"
msgstr "到底發生什麼事了？"

msgid "This beast, is trying to get us to sneak into its boss's hideout tonight. Says all the Golbins will be out escorting a shipment."
msgstr "這個畜生想要我們今晚潛入牠老大的藏身處。說所有哥布林都會出去護送一批貨。"

msgid "A shipment of..."
msgstr "一批什麼貨……"

msgid "...humans. That's what the Ringleader wants from all of the Golbin tribes he subjugates!"
msgstr "……人類。那就是首領從所有被他征服的哥布林部族那裡想要的東西！"

msgid "I told you that when you saved me from that group days ago!"
msgstr "幾天前你們把我從那群傢伙手中救出來時，我就告訴過你們了！"

msgid "What do you mean, saved you?"
msgstr "你說我們救了你，是什麼意思？"

msgid "I'm... little. Never been useful for much, the other Golbins said. Too 'so-fist-uh-cated', they'd say."
msgstr "我……很小隻。其他哥布林說我從來就沒什麼用。太「憂-雅」了，他們會這麼說。"

msgid "They were going to tie me up and try to put me in one of the shipments, too, since I wanted to 'act like a human'. "
msgstr "因為我想「表現得像個人類」，他們本來也要把我綁起來，想辦法把我塞進其中一批貨裡。 "

msgid "And why the blazes would they do that?"
msgstr "他們到底為什麼要那樣做？"

msgid "Because if a tribe doesn't pay up with enough people, the Ringleader takes his tithe in other ways. Turns us into ents. "
msgstr "因為如果一個部族交不出足夠的人，首領就會用其他方式收取貢品。把我們變成樹人。 "

msgid "Something about needing a creature's lifeforce. But I wasn't even ever part of that tribe, I got outcast from my own years ago."
msgstr "好像是需要生物的生命力什麼的。但我根本從來不屬於那個部族，我好幾年前就被自己的部族放逐了。"

msgid "And then they captured you again sometime after the Ringleader took over?"
msgstr "然後在首領接管之後，他們又抓到你了？"

msgid "Why were you in the group that attacked us, then?"
msgstr "那你為什麼會在襲擊我們的那群傢伙裡？"

msgid "One of the Golbin's fancied himself a knight and wanted to use me as a squire. Carry his weapons n' stuff."
msgstr "有隻哥布林自以為是騎士，想讓我當他的侍從。幫他扛武器之類的。"

msgid "We don't even have knights. But everyone thought it was funny, so they let him until it was going to be time to lump me in with a shipment."
msgstr "我們根本沒有騎士。但大家都覺得很好笑，所以就由著他，直到要把我塞進一批貨裡的時候。"

msgid "So... You've never even hurt a person?"
msgstr "所以……你從來沒傷害過人？"

msgid "No! I even traded with some of your people up north. I would make stuff, then sell it for books. I learned lots."
msgstr "沒有！我甚至跟你們北邊的人做過交易。我會做些東西，然後拿去換書。我學了很多。"

msgid "Jass... A moment?"
msgstr "Jass……借一步說話？"

msgid "You believe this little green booger, don't you?"
msgstr "你相信這隻綠色小鼻屎，對吧？"

msgid "You manage to pull Jass aside long enough to get her to calm down. She apologies, first to you, then even to Gloob, and says that when she learned that they were capturing people to 'send them somewhere' it sent her over the edge. She asks Gloob to fill you in on what he told her. Every full moon, a bunch of robed figures end up coming to the Ringleader's fortress within the Elder Grove. They come with large, wooden wagons, and leave with people that the surrounding Golbin tribes have captured.\n\nHe goes on to say that the Golbins at the fortress leave with the robed figures, escorting them... wherever they go, he doesn't know. With the nearing full-moon, it'd be a great chance to get a peek into the fortress, and that he'd even go, but that he'd need some climbing gear and hooks to scale the fort's outer wall. Either hopefully or foolishly, you decide to trust him, and he details how he'd go about making the equipment. You and Jass decide it'd be good to bring [Companion Name] along as well, and that they'd go over Gloob's memory of the fort to plan the scouting mission while you make the gear."
msgstr "你設法把 Jass 拉到一旁，讓她冷靜下來。她先向你道歉，接著甚至向 Gloob 道歉，說當她得知他們抓人是要「送去某個地方」時，她就失控了。她請 Gloob 把告訴她的事情跟你說一遍。每逢滿月，就會有一群穿長袍的人來到位於長老樹林中的首領堡壘。他們帶著大型木製篷車前來，離開時帶走周圍哥布林部族抓來的人。\n\n牠接著說，堡壘裡的哥布林會跟著那些長袍人一起離開，護送他們……至於去哪裡，牠也不知道。滿月將近，這會是窺探堡壘的大好機會，牠甚至願意一起去，但牠需要一些攀爬裝備和鉤子才能翻越堡壘的外牆。不知是懷抱希望還是愚蠢，你決定相信牠，牠也詳細說明了要如何製作這些裝備。你和 Jass 決定最好讓 [Companion Name] 也一起去，在你製作裝備的同時，由對方根據 Gloob 對堡壘的記憶來規劃偵察任務。"

msgid "You, Gloob, and [Companion Name] set off into the Misty Thicket on the night of the full moon. Gloob brings you through the woods quickly, and it's tough to keep up with his speed. You and [Companion Name] find yourselves huffing and puffing just outside of the Ringleader's Fortress. In the moonlight, you all see a train of wagons and hobgolbins heading to the north along an old dirt road, but quickly lose track of it as they slip into the dense thicket.\n\nWith them gone, the three of you use the gear you prepared and scale the walls, landing quietly on the other side. Gloob brings you to several spots throughout the relatively open grounds. A small, ramshackle prison, with several ents patrolling just outside. You pass by a handful of sleeping areas for the fort's living guards, until you reach a large wooden hut Gloob says is the Ringleader's home. Finally, he leads you to a stockpile of various bits that a Golbin would find valuable, taken as tribute or looted from nearby towns. Hides, half-rotten food, weapons and armor, gold, and most notably, dozens upon dozens of caskets of flammable oil and booze.\n\nYou and [Companion Name] wait for Gloob to lead you into an ambush, but the trap never comes. True to his word, once he finishes with the important parts of the fortress, the three of you scale back over the wall and head back to Azamire. When you return, you immediately begin talks with Jass about launching an assault on the fortress with what you've learned, and set plans into motion to get the town ready. Clearing a path to bring wagons to the fort, and securing an exit route for prisoners will be essential before launching an attack. Plus, it gives Jass more time to get her people ready, too."
msgstr "滿月之夜，你、Gloob 和 [Companion Name] 出發進入迷霧灌木林。Gloob 帶著你們快速穿越樹林，他的速度讓人很難跟上。你和 [Companion Name] 在首領堡壘外氣喘吁吁。在月光下，你們看到一列篷車和大哥布林沿著一條老舊的泥土路往北前進，但它們一鑽進茂密的灌木林，你們很快就失去了蹤影。\n\n他們離開後，你們三個用準備好的裝備翻過牆，悄悄落在另一側。Gloob 帶你們走過相對空曠的場地上的幾個地點。一座簡陋的小監獄，外面有幾個樹人在巡邏。你們經過幾處堡壘活人守衛的睡覺區，最後來到一間 Gloob 說是首領住所的大木屋。最後，牠帶你們來到一處堆放著各種哥布林眼中有價值之物的地方，都是作為貢品收取或從附近城鎮掠奪來的。獸皮、半腐爛的食物、武器和盔甲、金子，最引人注目的是，數十桶易燃的油和酒。\n\n你和 [Companion Name] 等著 Gloob 把你們帶進埋伏，但陷阱始終沒有出現。正如牠所說，在介紹完堡壘的重要部分後，你們三個翻回牆外，返回 Azamire。一回來，你們就立刻與 Jass 商討，根據所得情報對堡壘發動攻擊，並著手讓小鎮做好準備。在發動攻擊前，開闢一條讓篷車通往堡壘的道路，並確保囚犯有撤離路線，將是至關重要的。此外，這也讓 Jass 有更多時間讓她的人做好準備。"

msgid "Rocky Rumble"
msgstr "岩石轟隆"

msgid "The old Northern Road will take Azamire's wagons close to the Ringleader's Fortress, but due to a rockslide, it's unusable. With a bit of effort, it should be usable once again!"
msgstr "舊北方大道能讓 Azamire 的篷車接近首領的堡壘，但由於落石坍方，道路已無法通行。只要花點功夫，應該就能讓它恢復通行！"

msgid "Chisel first, then make them into volatile bombs. Easy."
msgstr "先鑿，再做成易爆的炸彈。簡單。"

msgid "Don't drop them don't drop them don't drop them."
msgstr "別掉了別掉了別掉了。"

msgid "Gloob - who is now allowed to freely roam the town after your scouting mission proved his loyalty - fetches you and brings you to Jass's newly constructed 'barracks'. In reality, it was just an enclosed room with some storage for gear and a few targets set up, but it was coming along nicely. Within her office, a map of the surrounding lands was laid out, recently purchased from one of the infrequent caravans that just started to come by once again."
msgstr "Gloob——在偵察任務證明了牠的忠誠後，現在獲准在鎮上自由走動——來找你，帶你到 Jass 新蓋好的「兵營」。實際上，那只是一個封閉的房間，有些存放裝備的空間和幾個靶子，但進展得很不錯。在她的辦公室裡，攤開著一張周邊地區的地圖，是最近從一支剛開始恢復往來、偶爾經過的商隊那裡買來的。"

msgid "Ah, [Player Name], you're here. We're planning our path to the fortress, but our scouts ran into a bit of a snag."
msgstr "啊，[Player Name]，你來了。我們正在規劃前往堡壘的路線，但我們的斥候遇到了一點麻煩。"

msgid "Oh? Is everyone alright?"
msgstr "噢？大家都還好嗎？"

msgid "No one is hurt. But a bit of the Old Northern Road that passes through the Foggy Canyon has been buried under a rock slide. "
msgstr "沒人受傷。但穿過霧谷的舊北方大道有一段被落石埋住了。 "

msgid "Then it seems we should just find another path, no?"
msgstr "那看來我們只要另找一條路就好了，不是嗎？"

msgid "That'd be great, but this is the only feasible way to bring wagons up to the fortress. We'll need them to carry gear, and... wounded, after the battle."
msgstr "那當然最好，但這是唯一能讓篷車通往堡壘的可行路線。我們需要篷車來運送裝備，還有……戰鬥後的傷患。"

msgid "Don't fret though! I know how to clear it! I just need a bit of help from you."
msgstr "不過別擔心！我知道怎麼清除它！只需要你幫點小忙。"

msgid "Just... you and me, clearing a rockslide? How well can you swing a pick?"
msgstr "就……你和我，去清除落石？你的鎬子揮得怎麼樣？"

msgid "No no, I have something far better."
msgstr "不不，我有更好的東西。"

msgid "Gloob gives you the rundown on an idea he's tried before. With a bit of effort, careful chiselling, and sulfur, fire runes could be made into shaped bombs could carefully carve a path through the rockslide. Not only that, he's actually already prepped some runes they traded for, but needs help with the chiselling and then... putting a bit more volatile fire energy into them."
msgstr "Gloob 向你簡述了一個他以前試過的點子。只要花點功夫、仔細鑿刻，再加上硫磺，就能把火焰符文做成定向炸彈，小心地在落石堆中炸出一條路。不只如此，他其實已經準備好一些換來的符文，但需要人幫忙鑿刻，然後……再往裡面注入更多不穩定的火焰能量。"

msgid "I don't suppose they're interested in talking this one out."
msgstr "我想他們應該沒興趣好好談一談。"

msgid "That seems like all of them, for now."
msgstr "目前看來應該全解決了。"

msgid "You carefully bring the volatile runes down to the Foggy Canyon along with Gloob and set to work tucking them into the rock. Gloob lights them as you move away, and sure enough, they work exceedingly well. Gloob stands triumphantly as bits of rock pelt the two of you after the series of explosions."
msgstr "你小心翼翼地帶著不穩定的符文，和 Gloob 一起來到霧谷，開始把它們塞進岩石中。你離開後 Gloob 點燃了它們，果然，效果好得驚人。一連串爆炸之後，碎石紛紛砸在你們兩個身上，Gloob 得意洋洋地站著。"

msgid "And that is why reading is cool! "
msgstr "這就是為什麼閱讀很酷！ "

msgid "Wait, what does this have to do with reading?"
msgstr "等等，這跟閱讀有什麼關係？"

msgid "I got the idea for these bombs after reading about a wizard that was banished from her family for blowing up half her estate. Tough luck, right?"
msgstr "我是讀到一個巫師因為炸掉半座莊園而被家族放逐的故事，才想到做這些炸彈的。運氣真差，對吧？"

msgid "Wow, do you think it was on purpose?"
msgstr "哇，你覺得她是故意的嗎？"

msgid "No clue! But it got me thinking about what happens when magic goes wrong, you know?"
msgstr "不知道！但這讓我開始思考，魔法出錯時會發生什麼事，你懂吧？"

msgid "I should... be a little more careful with fire spells in the future."
msgstr "我以後……使用火焰法術時應該小心一點。"

msgid "It's always good to practice caution! Shall we get back to bombing the crap out of this canyon now?"
msgstr "小心謹慎總是好事！那我們現在可以回去把這座峽谷炸個稀巴爛了嗎？"

msgid "Of course! It actually seems that some of the rocks are already moving out of the way in fear, should be a bit less to handle."
msgstr "當然！看起來有些石頭已經嚇得自己讓開了，應該可以少處理一些。"

msgid "Wait."
msgstr "等等。"

msgid "Why are the rocks moving?"
msgstr "石頭為什麼會動？"

msgid "As the question leaves your lips, several golems rise from the piles of rock, doubtlessly less than pleased with your explosive intrusion on their turf. They seem quite keen on smashing you into the ground so they can return to their nap."
msgstr "話才剛說出口，好幾個石像從碎石堆中站了起來，顯然對你們在牠們地盤上的爆炸入侵非常不滿。牠們似乎很想把你砸進地裡，好回去繼續睡午覺。"

msgid "Maybe I should ask someone in the mines..? Nah, what's the worst that could happen?"
msgstr "也許我該去礦坑問問人……？算了，最糟又能怎樣？"

msgid "I think that should hold!"
msgstr "我想這應該撐得住！"

msgid "The golems now lay crushed at your feet. Gloob held his own well, using his speed to distract them and a few carefully placed bombs to take out a few of his own. As the two of you catch your breath, one of the walls of the canyon cracks and Gloob jumps back and wraps himself around your leg in fear. A massive sheet of stone falls to the ground in front of you. After the dust settles, Gloob removes himself from your leg and clears his throat while dusting himself off."
msgstr "石像們如今已被擊碎，倒在你腳邊。Gloob 表現得很好，利用速度分散牠們的注意力，還用幾顆精準放置的炸彈解決了幾隻。就在你們倆喘口氣時，峽谷的一面岩壁裂開了，Gloob 嚇得往後一跳，緊緊抱住你的腿。一大片岩石在你們面前轟然落地。塵埃落定後，Gloob 從你腿上下來，一邊拍掉身上的灰，一邊清了清喉嚨。"

msgid "Well, uh... That's certainly not great."
msgstr "呃，嗯……這可真不妙。"

msgid "Shouldn't be hard to break up and move, but if the canyon walls keep collapsing, we'll hardly have a road left here at all."
msgstr "要把它敲碎搬走應該不難，但如果峽谷岩壁一直崩塌，這裡就根本不會剩下什麼路了。"

msgid "Or... Even worse, it could come down while people are travelling through. "
msgstr "或者……更糟的是，可能在有人經過時塌下來。 "

msgid "Then we've got to support the walls, yeah? I... haven't read much on building stuff like that, yet."
msgstr "那我們就得加固岩壁，對吧？我……還沒讀過多少關於蓋那種東西的書。"

msgid "[Companion Name] and I have actually helped out in Azamire's mines a few times through the years."
msgstr "其實這些年來，我和 [Companion Name] 在 Azamire 的礦坑幫過幾次忙。"

msgid "We'll need some rock bolts, which we can make out of steel, then we drive them into the walls."
msgstr "我們需要一些岩栓，可以用鋼來做，然後把它們打進岩壁裡。"

msgid "You walk Gloob through finding good spots for the bolts, and leave him to mark spots in the canyon that'll work well. Then you start to work out how to create strong enough rock bolts to keep the canyon walls from collapsing in on themselves."
msgstr "你教 Gloob 如何找到適合打岩栓的位置，讓他去峽谷裡標記合適的地點。接著你開始研究如何製作足夠堅固的岩栓，防止峽谷岩壁崩塌。"

msgid "The sides of the Foggy Canyon hold once you and Gloob finish up hammering the bolts into its walls. Even as you finish up blowing up the last of the rock that remains along the old Northern Road, your handiwork holds, and after you've finished your work, you no longer fear having a sheet of stone land on your head. You look down to the little Golbin by your hand who beams with pride at a job well done, ecstatic to have been able to put his mind to something and see something tangible come out. The two of you head back to Azamire to report a job well done, and that the Northern Road is clear to use once again."
msgstr "你和 Gloob 把岩栓錘進岩壁後，霧谷兩側便穩固了。就連你把舊北方大道上殘留的最後一點岩石炸掉時，你的成果依然屹立不搖，完工之後，你再也不用擔心會有一大片岩石掉到頭上。你低頭看著手邊的小哥布林，他為出色完成的工作感到自豪，能夠專心投入一件事並看到實際成果，讓他興奮不已。你們倆返回 Azamire，回報任務圓滿完成，北方大道再度可以通行。"

msgid "Dungeon Breakout"
msgstr "地城突圍"

msgid "A path must be cleared for the prisoners to get out of the Misty Thicket fortress when you launch the attack against the Ringleader, lest they get caught in the crossfire between you and the fortresses' guard."
msgstr "在你對首領發動攻擊時，必須為囚犯開闢一條逃出迷霧灌木林堡壘的路，以免他們被捲入你們與堡壘守衛之間的交火。"

msgid "Gold coins aren't good enough, eh?"
msgstr "金幣還不夠好，是吧？"

msgid "Hopefully Gloob's contacts pull through."
msgstr "希望 Gloob 的門路靠得住。"

msgid "The moon was completely hidden by clouds on the night you found yourself outside of the Ringleader's fortress, yet again. The scouting trips had gotten more frequent, though you only had time to go on a few of them lately. But Jass hadn't brought you out for a scouting mission, this time. The two of you wait for a patrol to pass and she brings you to the covered end of a tunnel. You two climb in and follow it for a while, until hitting what must be the wooden wall of the fortress. Gloob is crouched down here, inspecting the wall, not needing any light to see it clearly."
msgstr "在你再次來到首領堡壘外的那晚，月亮完全被雲層遮住。偵察行動越來越頻繁，不過你最近只有空參加其中幾次。但這次 Jass 帶你出來並不是為了偵察。你們等一支巡邏隊經過後，她帶你來到一條隧道被遮蓋起來的入口。你們爬進去走了一段時間，直到碰到應該是堡壘的木牆。Gloob 正蹲在這裡檢查牆壁，不需要任何光線就能看得一清二楚。"

msgid "Not sure how far down the wall goes, but we can't just dig down further."
msgstr "不確定這面牆往下延伸多深，但我們不能就這樣繼續往下挖。"

msgid "If it goes all the way down to stone, I wouldn't even know how start trying to get through the stone. I'm no rockhound."
msgstr "如果它一路延伸到岩層，我根本不知道該怎麼穿過岩石。我又不是採礦的。"

msgid "And forget about keeping it quiet. I know your people have been at this for a while, right? I'm sure moving all this soil is tough."
msgstr "更別提要保持安靜了。我知道你們的人已經做這件事一陣子了，對吧？搬這麼多土一定很辛苦。"

msgid "You'd bet. We've got to carry it all out and then sprinkle it through the woods. If a patrol came across a random pile of dirt, that'd be... suspicious."
msgstr "那還用說。我們得把土全部搬出去，然後撒在樹林裡。要是巡邏隊碰到一堆莫名其妙的土，那就……太可疑了。"

msgid "Makes sense. So, you need to get through this wall. Any ideas?"
msgstr "有道理。所以，你們需要穿過這面牆。有什麼想法嗎？"

msgid "Well, Gloob says he can get a tool to get through it... Right Gloob?"
msgstr "嗯，Gloob 說他能弄到一個穿牆的工具……對吧，Gloob？"

msgid "Yeah, I'm... know to locate some stuff, from time to time."
msgstr "對，我……偶爾能找到一些東西。"

msgid "I made a lot of contacts when I was traveling about. We'd have to trade for it."
msgstr "我四處旅行時結識了很多門路。我們得拿東西去換。"

msgid "What would you... contacts, want?"
msgstr "你的……門路，會想要什麼？"

msgid "Well, they typically deal in silver bars. I think it'd usually be about seven or eight bars, but this tool is special item."
msgstr "嗯，他們通常收銀錠。一般大概七、八錠，但這個工具是特別的物品。"

msgid "Let's say ten bars even."
msgstr "就算整數十錠吧。"

msgid "Ten it is."
msgstr "就十錠。"

msgid "You ask what the tool even is, and Gloob starts to describe a magical length of metal fashioned after a knife that, when activated, starts to vibrate rapidly. It should be enough to quietly carve away at the wall, albeit slowly. You leave Gloob to his inspection of the wall, and head off to get some silver."
msgstr "你問那到底是什麼工具，Gloob 開始描述一把仿造刀子形狀的魔法金屬條，啟動後會快速振動。雖然慢，但應該足以安靜地切開牆壁。你讓 Gloob 繼續檢查牆壁，自己出發去弄些銀錠。"

msgid "Just press it into the wall and cut, no problem."
msgstr "只要壓進牆裡切開就好，沒問題。"

msgid "I don't think anyone heard me."
msgstr "我想應該沒人聽到。"

msgid "You hand off the bars to Gloob back in Azamire, and not long after, he shows up on your doorstep, carrying a sheet wrapped around the vibrating knife he described. He happily hands it over."
msgstr "你回到 Azamire 把銀錠交給 Gloob，沒過多久，他就出現在你家門口，帶著一塊布包著他描述的那把振動刀。他開心地把刀交給你。"

msgid "Thankfully, it shouldn't take you too long to get through with this."
msgstr "還好有了這個，你應該不用花太久就能切穿。"

msgid "Just kinda... press it into the wood and it'll activate. I've marked the hole you need to cut in red paint, okay?"
msgstr "只要……把它壓進木頭裡，它就會啟動。我已經用紅漆標出你需要切的洞了，好嗎？"

msgid "Thank you, Gloob. This is really helpful. I know it might feel a bit odd helping us humans out, but I just wanted to let you know that we appreciate your help."
msgstr "謝謝你，Gloob。這真的很有幫助。我知道幫我們人類可能讓你覺得有點奇怪，但我只是想讓你知道，我們很感謝你的幫忙。"

msgid "I hope that folks aren't giving you too much trouble around town, are they?"
msgstr "希望鎮上的人沒給你添太多麻煩吧？"

msgid "Not at all, actually. Maybe a couple weird looks here and there, sure, but they've been more than welcoming."
msgstr "其實一點也沒有。當然，偶爾會有幾個怪異的眼神，但他們都非常歡迎我。"

msgid "Even your mayor! Sounds like he's going to try and get me set up with a workshop of sorts!"
msgstr "連你們的鎮長也是！聽起來他要幫我弄一間類似工坊的地方！"

msgid "Oh and I'm really starting to grow on Jass, and [Companion Name] is having me do a few things around, and also..."
msgstr "噢，還有 Jass 真的開始喜歡我了，[Companion Name] 也讓我幫忙做一些事，還有……"

msgid "Gloob starts to run through... more of his social life than you bargained for, and around the twenty minute mark you cough and mention that you really ought to get going to the fortress. Completely oblivious, he wishes you luck, and you set off. Back down at the end of the tunnel, sure enough, Gloob has marked a large cutout for you to follow."
msgstr "Gloob 開始滔滔不絕地講起……超出你預期的社交生活，大約二十分鐘後，你咳了一聲，說你真的該出發去堡壘了。他完全沒察覺，祝你好運，你便出發了。回到隧道盡頭，果然，Gloob 已經標出了一大塊要切割的區域。"

msgid "You're able to cut through the wall after a fair bit of effort, and finally, the chunk of wood settles. You set the tool down beside you and decide to leave it there, in case anyone needs to improve upon your work. Once you're done, you carefully leave the tunnel and cover the entrance once again, before reporting back to Jass. She sends for a few people to go continue with the rest of the tunnel and assures you that it'll be ready for when you need to get the prisoners out."
msgstr "費了好一番功夫，你終於切穿了牆，那塊木頭也落了下來。你把工具放在身旁，決定留在那裡，以防有人需要改進你的成果。完成後，你小心地離開隧道，再次遮蓋好入口，然後向 Jass 回報。她派了幾個人去完成剩下的隧道，並向你保證，等你需要救出囚犯時一定會準備好。"

msgid "Tree Trimming"
msgstr "修剪樹木"

msgid "[Companion Name] has been strangely absent lately, and on the rare chance you do see them, they usually quickly excuse themselves. What's going on?"
msgstr "[Companion Name] 最近奇怪地不見人影，難得見到對方時，對方通常也很快就找藉口離開。到底怎麼了？"

msgid "Good food always makes you feel better."
msgstr "美食總是能讓人心情變好。"

msgid "Maybe I should have gone for something more nutritious..."
msgstr "也許我該選更營養一點的東西……"

msgid "Late in the evening, you head to the recently built home for [Companion Name]. It's nothing fancy - like most of the new constructions in Azamire - but all of the folks who've been contributing the most were given priority in separate lodgings, and they've done wonders for bringing back a bit of normalcy.\n\nWhat hasn't been normal is how little you've seen [Companion Name] lately. You've had plenty of times where you weren't attached at the hip over the years you've known one another, but you know they've been around. It almost feels as if they've been avoiding you.\n\nYou knock several times to no avail. Just as you turn to go, you see a limping figure approach, notice you, and then turn away."
msgstr "深夜，你前往 [Companion Name] 新蓋好的家。那房子並不豪華——就像 Azamire 大多數的新建築一樣——但所有貢獻最多的人都被優先分配到獨立住所，這為找回一點日常生活帶來了奇蹟般的效果。\n\n不尋常的是，你最近很少見到 [Companion Name]。在你們相識的這些年裡，你們也有很多時候不是形影不離，但你知道對方一直都在附近。這次幾乎讓人覺得對方在躲著你。\n\n你敲了好幾次門，都沒有回應。就在你轉身要走時，你看到一個一瘸一拐的身影走近，發現了你，然後轉身離開。"

msgid "...[Companion Name]?"
msgstr "……[Companion Name]？"

msgid "Ohhhh..! Hello there, ol' buddy ol' pal. I'm just... gonna, go... this way..."
msgstr "噢噢噢……！嗨，我的好兄弟好夥伴。我只是……要，往……這邊走……"

msgid "Forgot that I needed to chat with... Hapren! That's right, needed to chat with Hapren."
msgstr "忘了我得去找……Hapren 聊聊！對，我得去找 Hapren 聊聊。"

msgid "[Companion Name], I'm not really sure what's going on, but if I did something, please... Let me know, okay?"
msgstr "[Companion Name]，我不太確定發生了什麼事，但如果我做了什麼，拜託……告訴我，好嗎？"

msgid "I didn't forget your birthday or anything, did I? I'm sorry, okay..?"
msgstr "我沒忘記你的生日之類的吧？對不起，好嗎……？"

msgid "[Player Name]..."
msgstr "[Player Name]……"

msgid "No, I've just been..."
msgstr "不，我只是一直在……"

msgid "I..."
msgstr "我……"

msgid "[Companion Name] turns towards you and wobbles on their feet. Even in the low light, you notice the dark red patch blood on the front of their cloak, and trailing down their arms. You rush towards them and manage to catch your best friend before they hit the ground. You quickly run through a list of places you could bring them before settling on their own place. You quickly fish their key out of their pocket and carry them inside. You'd complain about them being heavy if it weren't for the fact your heart was beating out of your chest, knowing how hurt they are and having no idea on why or how.\n\nDigging through both their supplies and yours, you find enough to get them patched up. Across their chest is a large gash with bits of... wood, sticking out of it? You extract it all, bit by bit, in the lantern light, and stitch them back up before wrapping them in gauze. The rest of their wounds are comparatively minor, and take much less time to deal with, but they are numerous, and in various states of healing, some old, some fresh.\n\nOnce you're done, [Companion Name] looks more mummy than person, but they'll live. You cover them up to let them rest, and decide to help along their recovery with their favorite food."
msgstr "[Companion Name] 轉向你，腳步搖搖晃晃。即使光線昏暗，你也注意到對方斗篷前方有一大片暗紅色的血跡，還沿著手臂往下流。你衝過去，在你最好的朋友倒地之前接住了對方。你迅速想過可以帶對方去哪些地方，最後決定就去對方家裡。你很快從對方口袋裡摸出鑰匙，把人扛了進去。要不是你的心臟跳得快要蹦出胸口——知道對方傷得多重，卻完全不知道原因和經過——你大概會抱怨對方很重。\n\n翻遍了對方和你自己的物資，你找到足夠的東西幫對方包紮。對方胸前有一道很大的傷口，上面插著一些……木頭碎片？你在提燈的光線下一點一點地把它們全部取出，縫合傷口後再用紗布包起來。其餘的傷相比之下都算輕微，處理起來快得多，但數量眾多，癒合程度也各不相同，有些是舊傷，有些是新傷。\n\n處理完後，[Companion Name] 看起來更像木乃伊而不是人，但性命無虞。你幫對方蓋好被子讓對方休息，並決定做對方最愛吃的食物來幫助康復。"

msgid "Time for a little bit of payback."
msgstr "該小小報復一下了。"

msgid "They're still... moving a bit."
msgstr "它們還在……稍微動著。"

msgid "[Companion Name] manages to quietly eat the cake you give them, and you decide to wait a while before beginning your round of questioning. Once they finish the first half, your questioning begins, and they fake passing out. You roll your eyes, and threaten to take the rest of the cake away and they spring back up, but quickly nurse their wounds after the sudden movement. You ask what happened, how they feel, and what they why they've been avoiding you, but [Companion Name] remains silent for all of it. When you finally ask why they didn't bring you, tears well up in their eyes."
msgstr "[Companion Name] 安靜地吃著你給的蛋糕，你決定等一會兒再開始盤問。等對方吃完一半，你開始提問，對方卻假裝昏倒。你翻了個白眼，威脅要把剩下的蛋糕拿走，對方立刻彈坐起來，但因為突然的動作而馬上護住傷口。你問發生了什麼事、感覺怎麼樣、為什麼一直躲著你，但 [Companion Name] 對每個問題都保持沉默。當你最後問對方為什麼不帶你一起去時，對方的眼眶湧出了淚水。"

msgid "I... I couldn't put you in danger, [Player Name]."
msgstr "我……我不能讓你陷入危險，[Player Name]。"

msgid "What do you mean, you couldn't put me in danger?"
msgstr "你說不能讓我陷入危險，是什麼意思？"

msgid "If you were doing something dangerous, then I especially should have been there!"
msgstr "如果你在做危險的事，那我更應該在場才對！"

msgid "What were you thinking?"
msgstr "你到底在想什麼？"

msgid "That I didn't want to lose you too!"
msgstr "我在想我不想連你也失去！"

msgid "That I had to keep Azamire safe and if I brought you with me, you might not come back!"
msgstr "我在想我必須保護 Azamire 的安全，如果帶你一起去，你可能就回不來了！"

msgid "We've already lost twenty more people on the route to the Ringleader's fortress in the past couple weeks."
msgstr "過去這幾週，我們在通往首領堡壘的路上又失去了二十個人。"

msgid "All but two of them were to a single weird ent. Way bigger than the rest, and covered in these weird... talismans."
msgstr "除了兩個人以外，全都是被同一個怪異的樹人殺死的。牠比其他樹人大得多，身上掛滿了奇怪的……護符。"

msgid "That's what did this to you?"
msgstr "你身上的傷就是那東西造成的？"

msgid "I didn't want to bring you in case... It had something we couldn't handle."
msgstr "我不想帶你去，以防……牠有我們應付不了的能力。"

msgid "We lost so much in the attack, but at least... I still had you. I couldn't lose you, too."
msgstr "我們在那次襲擊中失去了太多，但至少……我還有你。我不能連你也失去。"

msgid "So you tried to fight it on your own? [Companion Name] why-"
msgstr "所以你就想自己一個人跟牠打？[Companion Name]，為什麼——"

msgid "I just wanted to see it! I've been practicing on the smaller ones all this time."
msgstr "我只是想去看看牠！這段時間我一直在拿小隻的練習。"

msgid "Tonight, I figured that I could get a look at the big one, learn what it could do, come back to town, and come up with a plan against it."
msgstr "今晚，我想說可以去看看那隻大的，了解牠能做什麼，然後回鎮上想個對付牠的計畫。"

msgid "So... what happened?"
msgstr "所以……發生了什麼事？"

msgid "They detail the events of the night. How they came across the creature, and the talismans in its branches flashed with a bright blue light as they tried to run away. How they floated up into the air and were sucked towards the ent while they flailed about in the air, and then how the ent sent them flying after the talismans in its branches flashed bright blue. [Companion Name] was sure they were going to die, until they saw that the talismans in the ent's branches matched the similar charms forming a line in the nearby treeline. The giant ent shuffled back and forth at that line, but wouldn't cross it. Then, they limped all the way back to Azamire.\n\nAfter a through amount of ridicule and chastisement, you hug them and tell them you're glad they're okay.\n\nIn the morning you detail everything that happened to Jass, who gathers up the archers of her militia and send them out with you and a wounded [Companion Name], who leads you to the grove with the giant ent. It seems that it has been joined by several of the smaller ones, but you aren't dissuaded. "
msgstr "對方詳細描述了那晚發生的事。對方如何遇上那隻怪物，當對方試圖逃跑時，牠枝幹上的護符閃起刺眼的藍光。對方如何飄到半空中，在空中掙扎時被吸向樹人，接著在牠枝幹上的護符再次閃起藍光後，被樹人一擊打飛。[Companion Name] 本以為自己必死無疑，直到看見樹人枝幹上的護符，與附近林線上排成一列的類似符咒相符。巨大的樹人在那條線前來回挪動，卻不肯越過。之後，對方一路一瘸一拐地走回了 Azamire。\n\n在一番徹底的嘲笑和責備之後，你抱住對方，告訴對方你很高興對方平安無事。\n\n早上，你把發生的一切詳細告訴 Jass，她召集了民兵中的弓箭手，派他們和你以及負傷的 [Companion Name] 一起出發，由 [Companion Name] 帶你們前往巨大樹人所在的樹林。看來牠身邊多了幾隻較小的樹人，但你並沒有因此退縮。 "

msgid "Let's make them a bit smaller, turned into ash."
msgstr "讓牠們變小一點，燒成灰燼。"

msgid "Think that's everything!"
msgstr "我想就這些了！"

msgid "The ents are all down, and the archers do their best to shoot the talismans out of the trees incase they do... anything bad. [Companion Name] holds their bow at their side, pleased to have gotten a little payback, then kicks at an ent's branch that seems to be trying to crawl away."
msgstr "樹人全都倒下了，弓箭手們盡力把護符從樹上射下來，以防它們做出……什麼壞事。[Companion Name] 把弓垂在身側，很高興能小小報復了一下，接著踢了一腳一根似乎想爬走的樹人枝幹。"

msgid "Thank you... I'm sorry I tried to play the hero."
msgstr "謝謝你……對不起，我想逞英雄。"

msgid "If you didn't... I probably would have. I don't want to lose you either."
msgstr "如果你沒那麼做……我大概也會。我也不想失去你。"

msgid "Please, don't do something like that again, okay? I need you too."
msgstr "拜託，別再做那種事了，好嗎？我也需要你。"

msgid "Okay okay... You too, alright? Promise?"
msgstr "好啦好啦……你也是，好嗎？說好了？"

msgid "Promise."
msgstr "說好了。"

msgid "Me too."
msgstr "我也是。"

msgid "Seems the trees aren't quite 'dead' yet, huh?"
msgstr "看來這些樹還沒完全「死透」，是吧？"

msgid "Doubt they'll survive being turned into ash, don't you think?"
msgstr "我想牠們被燒成灰之後就活不了了吧？"

msgid "Everyone gathers up the ent parts. They don't seem dangerous anymore, but you do notice that - slowly but surely - they're starting to gain new growth. If you waited long enough, they'd likely become a threat again. The archers help by snapping off new branches and tossing them back into the pile, and occasionally making sure that none have managed to crawl away."
msgstr "大家把樹人的殘骸收集起來。它們看起來不再危險，但你確實注意到——緩慢而確實地——它們開始長出新的枝芽。如果等得夠久，它們很可能會再次成為威脅。弓箭手們幫忙折斷新長出的樹枝，把它們丟回堆裡，偶爾也確認沒有任何一塊爬走。"

msgid "The last bit of smoke goes out as the final pile of burning ent runs out of fuel. You were almost tempted to start trying to grill something, but the idea of the smoke being evil and getting into the food dissuaded any attempts. [Companion Name] leans against you, both for comfort, and because they are far from recovered from their wounds. You tease them lightly about getting smacked around by kindling, to which they reply by driving the butt of their bow into your foot. You tussel their hair and give them a hug, and tell them that you're glad they're safe."
msgstr "最後一堆燃燒的樹人燒盡時，最後一縷煙也散去了。你差點想試著烤點東西，但一想到那煙可能是邪惡的、會跑進食物裡，就打消了念頭。[Companion Name] 靠在你身上，一方面是為了安慰，一方面是因為傷勢還遠遠沒有痊癒。你輕輕調侃對方被柴火打得落花流水，對方則用弓柄戳了你的腳作為回應。你揉亂對方的頭髮，給了對方一個擁抱，告訴對方你很高興對方平安。"

msgid "In the Thick of It"
msgstr "深入其中"

msgid "Azamire is as ready as it ever will be to take down the Ringleader. The old Northern Road is clear, Jass's crew has finished the tunnel to the prison, and you have defeated the worst of the Misty Thicket's roaming guards. Now, all that's left to do is burn the fortress to the ground."
msgstr "Azamire 已經做好了擊垮首領的萬全準備。舊北方大道已經暢通，Jass 的團隊完成了通往監獄的隧道，你也擊敗了迷霧灌木林中最難纏的巡邏守衛。現在，只剩下把堡壘燒成平地了。"

msgid "If I want any supplies, I should take them from the cart before the attack starts in earnest."
msgstr "如果我需要任何補給，應該在攻擊正式開始前從推車上拿。"

msgid "It's time."
msgstr "時候到了。"

msgid "As you walk through Azamire, the town is abuzz with nervous energy. Several wagons are lined up and everyone who isn't fighting have come out to wish you well. Hapren approaches, and mentions that the town has gotten together and prepared some combat supplies into the back of one of the carts for you, and hopes that it helps.\n\nYou all set off, and as the sun begins to set, the cold mist of the thicket starts to seep into your clothes. The militia is tense, but ready. There are people to save, and taking out the Ringleader would go a long way towards making everyone safer."
msgstr "當你走過 Azamire 時，整個小鎮瀰漫著緊張的氣氛。幾輛篷車排成一列，所有不參戰的人都出來為你們送行。Hapren 走過來，說鎮上的人一起在其中一輛推車後面為你準備了些戰鬥補給，希望能派上用場。\n\n你們出發了，太陽開始西沉時，灌木林冰冷的霧氣開始滲進你的衣服。民兵們很緊張，但已做好準備。有人等著被救，而除掉首領將大大有助於讓所有人更安全。"

msgid "Everyone's ready?"
msgstr "大家都準備好了嗎？"

msgid "Let's get this done."
msgstr "我們把事情解決吧。"

msgid "Don't have any qualms with this, Gloob?"
msgstr "對這件事沒有任何顧慮嗎，Gloob？"

msgid "I might be green, but I'm no Golbin. Let's take him out."
msgstr "我也許是綠色的，但我可不是那種哥布林。我們去幹掉他。"

msgid "You okay, [Player Name]?"
msgstr "你還好嗎，[Player Name]？"

msgid "Never better. Plan is the same, still?"
msgstr "好得很。計畫還是一樣嗎？"

msgid "That's right. The tunnel under the prison is ready to get the prisoners out, and we'll have people posted at the exit."
msgstr "沒錯。監獄下方的隧道已經準備好讓囚犯逃出，我們會派人守在出口。"

msgid "As soon as people start escaping down the tunnel, the guards will notice everyone's missing and sound the alarm."
msgstr "一旦有人開始從隧道逃走，守衛就會發現人不見了並拉響警報。"

msgid "Once that happens, archers will try to hit that stockpile you mentioned with flaming arrows."
msgstr "一旦發生這種情況，弓箭手就會試著用火箭射中你說的那個物資堆。"

msgid "Should deal with most of the ents inside, and make a ton of noise. You'll be providing the fire, of course, we need several braziers lit."
msgstr "這應該能解決裡面大部分的樹人，還能製造一大堆噪音。當然，火就由你負責，我們需要點燃好幾座火盆。"

msgid "After that, we head to the gate and hack it down. The archers will keep us covered."
msgstr "之後，我們前往大門把它砍倒。弓箭手會掩護我們。"

msgid "And then we're in. Try to avoid the fire, and head for the Ringleader?"
msgstr "然後我們就進去了。盡量避開火，直奔首領？"

msgid "Exactly. Can't miss 'em. Big blue fella, covered in every gaudy fabric he fancies."
msgstr "沒錯。不會認錯的。藍色的大塊頭，身上披滿了他喜歡的各種俗氣布料。"

msgid "Things are going to get really hectic once this starts."
msgstr "一旦開始，場面會變得非常混亂。"

msgid "Stay safe, everyone."
msgstr "大家都要注意安全。"

msgid "You too, [Player Name]. You too."
msgstr "你也是，[Player Name]。你也是。"

msgid "As you finish your conversation, the fortress's outer wall comes into view. Gloob and small group of the militia break off and head for the tunnel while the rest of you set up on the hillside just outside. Several braziers are set up, and everyone starts to load them with wood while you and [Companion Name] get to work."
msgstr "當你們結束對話時，堡壘的外牆映入眼簾。Gloob 和一小群民兵脫隊前往隧道，其餘的人則在外面的山坡上就位。幾座火盆已經架好，大家開始往裡面添木頭，你和 [Companion Name] 則開始動手。"

msgid "We have to get through this gate!"
msgstr "我們必須突破這道門！"

msgid "There! A hole!"
msgstr "那裡！有個洞！"

msgid "Alarms start to sound as the militia's arrows are lit. You clutch your weapon in anticipation, wishing you could to go check on the tunnel to see how Gloob's breakout went, but there's no time. The hillside is lit up with the fires you and [Companion Name] started, and hobgolbins on the wall begin to shoot towards you. But it's too late. Burning arrow after arrow soar up and over the wall, towards where you pointed out the stockpile. No one can see over the wall, so it's tough to tell if anyone is on target until a resounding BOOM make you cover your ears, even from this far away.\n\nMany of the defenders are thrown from the wall entirely, and as you and the militia charge, the swordsmen dispatch the stunned hobgolbins that fell on the wrong side of the wall. Arrows start to fall again, as the fort's guards gather themselves, and they're met with your militia's own volleys."
msgstr "民兵的箭被點燃時，警報聲開始響起。你緊握武器蓄勢待發，真希望能去隧道看看 Gloob 的突圍進行得如何，但沒時間了。山坡被你和 [Companion Name] 點燃的火光照亮，牆上的大哥布林開始朝你們射擊。但已經太遲了。一支又一支燃燒的箭矢越過城牆，飛向你指出的物資堆位置。沒人能看到牆後的情況，所以很難判斷是否有人命中，直到一聲響亮的「轟」讓你即使在這麼遠的地方也得摀住耳朵。\n\n許多守衛直接被震下城牆，當你和民兵衝鋒時，劍士們解決了那些摔落到牆外、被震暈的大哥布林。隨著堡壘守衛重整旗鼓，箭雨再次落下，迎接它們的是你們民兵的齊射。"

msgid "FOR AZAMIRE!"
msgstr "為了 Azamire！"

msgid "Don't stop running until you hit the gate! "
msgstr "衝到大門之前都別停下來！ "

msgid "We can do this! Push on!"
msgstr "我們做得到！繼續前進！"

msgid "You and [Companion Name] reach the gate first and take out your axes, followed by a small group of other militia members who follow suit and get to work. Another group comes with large shields that they hold with both hands, more table than shield. But they work well as the shield group form a defensive shell around you and overhead, giving you room to work without worrying about an arrow finding its way in your unprotected back."
msgstr "你和 [Companion Name] 第一個抵達大門，拿出斧頭，隨後一小群民兵也跟著動手。另一群人帶著需要雙手持握的大盾牌趕來，與其說是盾牌，不如說更像桌子。但效果很好，盾牌隊在你周圍和頭頂組成一道防禦外殼，讓你有空間工作，不必擔心有箭射進你毫無防護的背後。"

msgid "We will not fall. Not this time."
msgstr "我們不會倒下。這次絕不會。"

msgid "It's... done."
msgstr "結……結束了。"

msgid "The occasional pained grunt, or worse, the painted gurgles of someone who was struck somewhere lethal, dampen your mood. You knew people would fall today. You can only imagine how the people on the hillside are faring. Just as your mind starts to lose focus, thinking about those you'd lose, you see a burning light at the end of your axe. As you pull it back, you realize you're through! You give a cheer that turns into a battlecry, and your group follows suit. A few more axe strikes and enough holes are opened to let Azamire's troops push through the gate.\n\nThe fort grounds are... hellish. Most of the ent guardians already crawl on the ground, crying out with groaning wails as they burn, with nearly every structure already completely engulfed in flames. You wonder for a moment if there's even a point of being inside until a massive blue Golbin covered in singed fabric cries out as he locks eyes with you. The rest of the fort's surviving defenders stand in the middle of the blazing stronghold with the Ringleader, smashing weapons against their shields, waiting for orders. "
msgstr "偶爾傳來的痛苦悶哼，或更糟的——某人被擊中要害時發出的咯咯聲，讓你的心情愈發沉重。你早知道今天會有人倒下，也只能想像山坡上的人們情況如何。正當你的思緒開始渙散，想著那些你將失去的人時，你看見斧頭盡頭透出一道燃燒的光芒。當你將斧頭抽回，你發現自己砍穿了！你發出一聲歡呼，隨即化為戰吼，你的隊伍也跟著齊聲吶喊。再砍幾斧，打開的缺口已足以讓 Azamire 的部隊衝過大門。\n\n要塞內部宛如……地獄。大多數樹人守衛早已在地上爬行，燃燒中發出呻吟般的哀號，幾乎每座建築都已被烈焰完全吞噬。你一時懷疑進來是否還有意義，直到一隻披著燒焦布料的巨大藍色 哥布林 與你四目相對，發出怒吼。要塞其餘倖存的守軍與首領一同站在熊熊燃燒的據點中央，用武器敲擊著盾牌，等待命令。 "

msgid "Humans want to be hand delivered to masters?"
msgstr "人類想被親手送到主人那裡？"

msgid "Ringleader need new stock, others just ran out."
msgstr "首領需要新貨，其他的剛用完。"

msgid "Come to me. Time for you to die."
msgstr "過來。你的死期到了。"

msgid "Keep the rest of them off [Player Name] and [Companion Name]! "
msgstr "別讓其他人靠近 [Player Name] 和 [Companion Name]！ "

msgid "Know that we fight not just for those back home, not just to save yourselves..."
msgstr "要知道，我們不只是為了家鄉的人而戰，也不只是為了拯救自己……"

msgid "But for everyone we've lost!"
msgstr "更是為了我們失去的每一個人！"

msgid "Together! Go! Now! Kill them all!"
msgstr "一起上！衝啊！現在！殺光他們！"

msgid "[Player Name], I'm with you. Trust me! I'll keep you safe!"
msgstr "[Player Name]，我與你同在。相信我！我會保護你的！"

msgid "Not a single person falters as they stream past you, charging with weapons and heads held high. You don't turn away as you see some being driven through as the Ringleader's forces crash into your own. Time slows as you push through, trusting your people to keep you safe. As you make it through the bodies, the Ringleader stands with a gnarled smirk, holding what must be half a burning tree as its weapon, seemingly unbothered by the flames that flicker up its arm.\n\nYou hear people roar in the battle behind you, some in victory, others... likely as their last act of defiance against the opposing force. You steel yourself and step forward, challenging the Ringleader."
msgstr "當眾人從你身旁湧過，沒有一個人退縮，他們揮舞著武器、昂首向前衝鋒。當首領的部隊與你們的人馬撞在一起，你看見有人被刺穿，但你沒有別過頭去。時間彷彿變慢了，你奮力向前推進，相信你的同伴會保護你。當你穿過人群，首領帶著扭曲的獰笑站在那裡，手持一截似乎是燃燒中的半棵樹作為武器，對沿著手臂竄升的火焰似乎毫不在意。\n\n你聽見身後的戰場上傳來陣陣怒吼，有些是勝利的吶喊，有些……恐怕是對抗敵軍的最後一搏。你穩住心神，向前踏出一步，向首領發起挑戰。"

msgid "Before you lies the broken body of the Ringleader, sickly purple blood spilling from his wounds. You finally spare a glance to those around you, and you realize... it's over. Less than half the attacking force remains, but Azamire's people still stand.  Gloob stands among the militia, deep green body covered in the blue blood of hobgolbins, and he lets out a cheer, one that the remaining militia proudly meet. Jass barks out orders, pointing out wounded with the stump of her arm, then starting to pull one of the wounded towards the gate with her other.\n\nHalf a dozen emotions cross [Companion Name]'s face the second you look at them, but most among them all, relief. They embrace you for naught but a moment before heading towards the Ringleader, who barely manages a ragged breath. As you approach, the beast lets out a throaty cackle before it devolves into a choking cough. You ask it two questions. Where did the shipments go, and who are the people it works for?\n\nHe just sits and smirks, the flames of his burning fortress dancing in his eyes.\n\n\"They'll come back soon.\""
msgstr "首領殘破的身軀倒在你面前，病態的紫色血液從傷口湧出。你終於有空環顧四周，然後意識到……結束了。進攻的部隊剩下不到一半，但 Azamire 的人們依然屹立。Gloob 站在民兵之中，深綠色的身體沾滿了大哥布林的藍色血液，他發出一聲歡呼，倖存的民兵也驕傲地回應。Jass 大聲下達命令，用斷臂指出傷患，接著用另一隻手將一名傷者拖向大門。\n\n當你望向 [Companion Name]，對方臉上閃過好幾種情緒，但其中最多的是如釋重負。他們短暫地擁抱了你一下，隨即走向奄奄一息、幾乎喘不過氣的首領。當你們走近，那頭野獸發出一陣沙啞的狂笑，隨後變成嗆咳。你問了牠兩個問題：那些貨物運到哪裡去了？牠替誰賣命？\n\n牠只是坐著冷笑，燃燒要塞的火光在牠眼中跳動。\n\n「他們很快就會回來。」"

